IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nba-types`

-- Nationality and Borders Act 2022 (UK) — GOAL 3: PRIORITY REMOVAL NOTICES
-- AND LATE EVIDENCE (ss 20-22, 26).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-2022-36.txt.

§ `Goal 3 — notices and late evidence`

-- ss 20(5), 22(7), 26(4)-(5): material or evidence is provided late if it
-- is provided "on or after" the cut-off date (or the date specified in an
-- evidence notice). s 20(4): not for anything provided before.
@ref ss 20(4)-(5), 22(7), 26(3)-(5)
@export Whether material was provided late in response to a priority removal notice (s 20) or an evidence notice (s 18) under the Nationality and Borders Act 2022 (UK): provided on or after the cut-off date, and not something already provided before the notice. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN n IS A `Notice facts`  @desc The cut-off date, when the material was provided, and whether it had already been provided
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the material was provided late under` n IF
    CONSIDER n's `material provided on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST d  THEN
            d AT LEAST n's `cut-off date`
        AND NOT (n's `previously provided`)

-- s 21(1) "A priority removal notice remains in force until the end of the
-- period of 12 months beginning with— (a) the PRN cut-off date, or (b) if
-- later, the day on which any appeal rights of the PRN recipient in respect of
-- a relevant claim are exhausted." The period ends on the day before the
-- corresponding date 12 months later, or the last day of that month if it
-- has none.
@ref s 21(1), (3)-(4)
@export The last day a priority removal notice remains in force under s 21(1) of the Nationality and Borders Act 2022 (UK): the end of the 12 months beginning with the later of the PRN cut-off date and the day appeal rights on a relevant claim are exhausted; NOTHING for an evidence notice. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN n IS A `Notice facts`  @desc The kind of notice, the cut-off date, and when appeal rights were exhausted
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day the priority removal notice is in force for` n MEANS
    CONSIDER n's `kind`
    WHEN `an evidence notice` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a priority removal notice` THEN JUST (`the last day of the 12 months beginning with` start)
    WHERE
        start MEANS
            CONSIDER n's `appeal rights exhausted on`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN n's `cut-off date`
            WHEN JUST e  THEN `the later of` (n's `cut-off date`) e
        GIVEN x IS A DATE
        GIVETH A DATE
        `the last day of the 12 months beginning with` x MEANS
            IF   DATE_DAY c EQUALS DATE_DAY x
            THEN `the day before` c
            ELSE c
            WHERE
                c MEANS `add months` x 12

-- s 20(7): a PRN recipient providing material late "must also provide a
-- statement setting out their reasons".
@ref s 20(5)-(7)
GIVEN n IS A `Notice facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a statement of reasons for lateness is required under` n IF
        `the material was provided late under` n
    AND isPRN
    WHERE
        isPRN MEANS
            CONSIDER n's `kind`
            WHEN `a priority removal notice` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 22(4) "a deciding authority must take account, as damaging the PRN
-- recipient's credibility, of the late provision of the material, unless
-- there are good reasons why it was provided late." (1)(c), (3): a relevant
-- decision is being made.
@ref s 22(1)-(4)
@export Whether the deciding authority must take late provision of material as damaging the PRN recipient's credibility under s 22 of the Nationality and Borders Act 2022 (UK): material provided late in response to a priority removal notice, a relevant decision being made, and no good reasons for the lateness. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN n IS A `Notice facts`  @desc The notice, the dates, whether a relevant decision is being made, and whether there were good reasons
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `lateness must be taken as damaging credibility under` n IF
        `a statement of reasons for lateness is required under` n
    AND n's `a relevant decision is being made`
    AND NOT (n's `good reasons for lateness`)

-- s 26(2) "Unless there are good reasons why the evidence was provided late,
-- the deciding authority must, in considering it, have regard to the
-- principle that minimal weight should be given to the evidence." (1)(b):
-- only where the evidence falls to be considered in determining the claim or
-- an appeal; the s 22(3) "relevant decision" input stands for that (added
-- after the independent pass, L256).
@ref s 26(1)-(5)
@export Whether the deciding authority must have regard to the principle that minimal weight should be given to evidence under s 26 of the Nationality and Borders Act 2022 (UK): evidence provided late under an evidence notice or a priority removal notice, and no good reasons for the lateness. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN n IS A `Notice facts`  @desc The notice, the dates, and whether there were good reasons
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `minimal weight applies to the evidence under` n IF
        `the material was provided late under` n
    AND n's `a relevant decision is being made`
    AND NOT (n's `good reasons for lateness`)
